    description: "Split from WI-mozig (concept audit 2026-10-21/22 F6; premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7). One field name, two meanings: IoPrimitive.requires_target_kind holds a TARGET KIND (std_stream; io_boundary.py:862, used once at java.yaml:401), while TaintSource/TaintSink.requires_target_kind holds a BOUNDARY (taint.py:299, :382; derived :2161-2165, :2180, :2212; compared :1234-1237). TaintSink.requires_mode also holds a boundary (taint.py:2196-2198). Pure rename on the taint side (e.g. requires_boundary), no behaviour change; update readers and tests."  # d327
